{
  "_README": "Kit template — copy to .claude/settings.json to ACTIVATE the Claude Code hooks (they execute shell commands on tool use / session start, so activation is a deliberate operator decision). The git-level commit-prefix guard (scripts/githooks/commit-msg) is wired separately via `git config core.hooksPath scripts/githooks` (setup.sh does this) and does NOT depend on this file.",

  "_PLACEHOLDERS": {
    "_note": "Replace every <angle-bracket> token below before copying this file to .claude/settings.json. The initializer stamps the first two; the rest are yours. Then DELETE this _PLACEHOLDERS block — Claude Code ignores unknown keys, but a stale placeholder map is a lie waiting to be read.",
    "<trunk>": "The single trunk branch. Default: main.",
    "<PREFIX>": "The issue-id prefix (scripts/config.sh ISSUE_PREFIX). Appears in branch names below.",
    "<code-path-globs>": "The comma-separated globs that count as CODE in this project — the paths that MUST go through a work branch and land via ./scripts/finish-pr.sh, never direct to the trunk. The adapter's 'what counts as CODE here' section is the source of truth; keep the two in sync. Example shape: src/**, tests/**, <the build/dependency manifest>.",
    "<metadata-path-globs>": "The globs that are metadata and MAY commit direct to the trunk with a role-prefixed subject. Everything the project treats as not-code. Example shape: progress/**, requirements/**, docs/**, dev/**, process/**, progress.md, <project-facts>, <adapter>, .claude/**, scripts/**, setup.sh, .gitignore.",
    "<adapter>": "The project-adapter filename Claude auto-loads at session start. Default: CLAUDE.md.",
    "<project-facts>": "The project-facts filename (stack, gates, credentials, build order). Default: PROJECT.md.",
    "<role-prefix-list>": "The bracketed role prefixes the commit-msg hook accepts. Must match the adapter's role-attribution table exactly. The kit's shipped set is [PM], [QA], [Dev], [Refactorer], [Orchestrator], [Architect] and [UIDesigner] — the last one is ACCEPTED BY THE SHIPPED HOOK even though its role doc ships parked, deliberately, so waking that role costs no hook change. Derive the set from scripts/githooks/commit-msg rather than trusting this list; it is one of several places the role set is written and therefore among the likeliest to drift, and process/EXTRACTION.md \u00a7 2.4's table is the list."
  },

  "_WHAT_THIS_FILE_MAY_CONTAIN": "ONLY SETTINGS KEYS WHOSE EFFECT THE KIT CAN DEMONSTRATE. This file used to carry an `autoMode` block (prose `allow`/`soft_deny`/`environment` lists describing direct-to-trunk authorization) and a `plansDirectory` value. Both were removed, and no verification of the host's settings schema was needed to decide it: NOTHING IN THE KIT READ EITHER KEY, the `autoMode` arrays held English sentences rather than tool patterns so no permission engine could enforce them under any key name, and this file's own note says unknown keys are ignored. So it enforced nothing AND guided nobody — a settings file is never read into an agent's context — while reading exactly like active authorization policy, which is the one thing an adopter would believe. The rule generalizes: if the kit cannot show what a key does, the kit does not ship it. Add a key here only alongside the thing that reads it.",

  "_WHERE_THE_TRUNK_POLICY_ACTUALLY_LIVES": "The adapter (CLAUDE.md) § 'The trunk, the branches, and what counts as code here', which cites process/MANUAL.md § The code-vs-metadata rule. Both are documents an agent actually reads. The deleted `autoMode` prose was a THIRD copy of that rule; it is not reproduced here, because a third copy is what drifts.",

  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Edit|Write|NotebookEdit",
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/scripts/hooks/require-role.sh\"" }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/scripts/hooks/session-start.sh\"" }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Notification": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/scripts/notify-hook.sh\"" }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
